    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Jrn2KurzT78udU8WM5CSmZ)_\n\n## What\nReplaces the Denote commands I liked, in `sp-notes`:\n- `sp-notes-create` (`SPC n c`, like `denote-create-note`): asks for a title and registered tags, writes the note with `:ID:` and `:CREATED:`, visits it. With tags it is written straight into its filing folder (same rules as the tag filing); without tags it stays at the top of the root, as the filing mode leaves it.\n- `sp-notes-open` (`SPC n o`, like `denote-open`): `completing-read` over every org file in all subfolders of the notes root. Each candidate is the file name with creation date, tags and title beside it, newest first. Dot folders, `ltximg/`, `attach/` and `data/` are not listed (`sp-notes-open-exclude-regexp`); inbox, area, log and workbook are.\n- `:CREATED:` on new notes: added in `sp-org--write-note` (new optional DIR arg and `sp-org-created-stamp`), so person and literature notes made through it get it too.\n\n## Ambiguity: where `:CREATED:` goes\n- Read as: the file-level property drawer beside `:ID:`, format `[2026-11-07 20:15]` (inactive timestamp, no weekday). It is what `sp-quick-capture`, `vulpea-para` and `sp-org-issues` already write.\n- Date shown by `sp-notes-open`: `:CREATED:`, else the id in the file name, else the modification time, so old notes without it still sort.\n- Not changed: notes made by `vulpea-create` (`vulpea-find`, inbox tab). Say if you want `vulpea-create-default-function` to add it too.\n- ADR 0025 (`-dryrun`/`-convert`) does not apply: these commands do not preview or convert anything.\n\n## Testing\n- 15 ERT tests pass in batch Emacs 29.3 (4 new: stamp format, create writes `:CREATED:` and files by tag, open info/candidates/annotation, date from file name); the author-notes and litnotes-meta tests still pass. Docs tangle to the committed `.el`.\n- /untested/ on the Mac, in the real vault, with real vulpea or in the GUI (vertico look of the picker annotations).\n- No CHANGELOG edit.\n\nLiterate doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-notes.org` and `sp-org-link-conversion.org` updated (bullet lists).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCRS63XsqDodY3EZBP)_",
